 "issue_title": "**Fake transfer-matrix** `coating_designer.py:135-148`",
 "issue_body": " computes dead `phases`, then incoherent `\u03a3r\u1d62\u00b2/len`.\n   No `M\u2c7c=[[cos\u03b4,i\u00b7sin\u03b4/\u03b7],[i\u03b7\u00b7sin\u03b4,cos\u03b4]]`.\n   BK7/MgF\u2082 QW gives 0.92% vs exact 1.28% (~30% low); off-design unbounded.\n   Angled branch `return 0.04`, `:150`, is a stub ignoring \u03b8 and s/p.",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/249",
 "pr": 267,
 "pr_title": "fix(coating): implement exact transfer-matrix reflectivity with angle\u2026",
 "pr_body": "\u2026d incidence\r\n\r\nReplace the incoherent interface-sum estimate (dead phase terms, normalization by layer count) with the characteristic-matrix method M_j=[[cos d,i sin d/eta],[i eta sin d,cos d]], Snell-corrected tilted admittances, s/p averaging for unpolarized light. Uncoated branch is now angle-aware Fresnel; oblique angles validated (Brewster Rp=0, MgF2 QW on BK7 = 1.2835% vs exact 1.284%).\r\n\r\nUpdate the e2e broadband assertion to the exact-physics value: the heuristic QW-pair dual stack averages ~5.4% over 450-650nm, not the ~2.4% the old formula returned. Add TestTransferMatrixPhysics with closed-form regression values.",
 "fix_commit": "ead039d33f8e8bee2d2c4a7233b500177dc5a749",
